---
import TopicLayout from "../layouts/TopicLayout.astro";
import changes from "../data/reviewed-changes.json";
import { loadMirror } from "../lib/mirror";
import { dateLabel } from "../lib/facts";
import { sourceLinkedEvents } from "../lib/research-events";
const mirror = await loadMirror();
const events = sourceLinkedEvents(mirror.facilities.facilities, mirror.events.events);
---
<TopicLayout title="Data Center Power Changes: Permits & Projects | BTW" description="Source-linked project changes with before-and-after fields, event dates, interpretation and next checks. Includes Abilene's permitted turbine revision." path="/changes/" heading="What changed in data center power?" deck="A reviewed change log connects a dated document to the field it changes, the implication and the next record to check.">
  <section class="topic-section wrap">
    <p>This edition contains {changes.length} interpreted entries, reviewed October 27, 2026 and ordered by event date. It includes retrospective milestones and filing metadata explicitly marked where document contents remain unread. Collection dates do not establish new physical events.</p>
    <p><a href="/research/opsb-review-2026-10/">OPSB: exact 44-record batch, supported findings and pending source-file review</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="#abilene-permit-revision-20250122">See Abilene's before-and-after example</a> · <a href="#published-events">Latest published record events</a> · <a href="/api/v1/changes.json">Download changes JSON</a></p>
  </section>
  {changes.map(change => <article class="topic-section wrap change-entry" id={change.id}>
    <p class="change-date"><time datetime={change.event_date}>{dateLabel(change.event_date)}</time> · {change.kind}</p>
    <h2>{change.title}</h2><p><a href={change.project_path}>{change.project}</a> · Reviewed <time datetime={change.reviewed_at}>{change.reviewed_at}</time></p>
    <p>{change.summary}</p>
    {change.changes.length > 0 && <div class="topic-table" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label={`${change.project} before and after`}><table><caption>Earlier evidence and the source-backed update</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Before</th><th scope="col">After</th></tr></thead><tbody>{change.changes.map(row => <tr><td>{row.field}</td><td>{row.before}</td><td>{row.after}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>}
    <div class="topic-two"><div><h3>Why it matters</h3><p>{change.meaning}</p></div><div><h3>What is still unknown</h3><p>{change.unknown}</p></div></div>
    <h3>Next check</h3><p>{change.next}</p><ul class="topic-source-list">{change.sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></li>)}</ul>
    {change.id.startsWith("abilene-") && <p><a href="/research/abilene-power-brief/">Read the full Abilene sample memo</a></p>}
  </article>)}
  <section class="topic-section wrap" id="published-events"><h2>Latest source-linked record events</h2><p>These events have a source URL and an existing published facility dossier. They refresh with site exports. Review events describe a check; they do not necessarily establish a physical change. Unreviewed collector candidates never appear here.</p><div class="published-events">{events.slice(0,12).map((event: any) => <article><p class="change-date">{dateLabel(event.date)} · {event.type.replaceAll("_"," ")}</p><p>{event.headline}</p><p><a href={`/facility/${event.facility}/`}>Facility record</a> · <a href={event.source_url}>Event source</a></p></article>)}</div><p class="topic-small">Mirror export: {mirror.summary.as_of}. <a href="/api/v1/events.json">Full events archive, including entries without source links</a> · <a href="/#coverage">Collection coverage and limits</a></p></section>
  <section class="topic-section wrap"><h2>How does a candidate become a published change?</h2><ol><li>Collect a public record and preserve its identity and date.</li><li>Review the project, phase, evidence basis and affected fields.</li><li>Publish the supported finding with source links, interpretation and unknowns.</li></ol><p>The interpreted entries above are a manually reviewed edition. Filing metadata is distinguished from completed document-content review. The published-event section updates from the mirror; interpretation is not published automatically from every registry hit.</p></section>
</TopicLayout>
<style>.change-entry{scroll-margin-top:24px}.change-date{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);margin-bottom:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.published-events article{padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.published-events p+p{margin-top:10px}</style>
